IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ky-income-tax`

-- KRS chapter 141 -- the seat of the individual taxpayer.
--
-- "Am I a Kentucky resident? What is my Kentucky AGI? Must I file? By when? How much do I owe, or get back? How much of
-- my tax does the family size credit take away?" Every answer is built from the rules in ky-income-tax.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Kentucky income tax -- my questions`

§§ `Am I a resident`

@export Am I a Kentucky resident for income tax (KRS 141.010(32))?
GIVEN `Kentucky is my domicile` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Kentucky is your domicile, your permanent home
      `I keep a place to live in Kentucky` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you maintain a place of abode in Kentucky
      `days I spent in Kentucky this year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of the tax year, in total, you spent in Kentucky
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a Kentucky resident` IF
    `is a resident` `Kentucky is my domicile` `I keep a place to live in Kentucky` `days I spent in Kentucky this year`

§§ `My Kentucky income`

@export What is my Kentucky adjusted gross income (KRS 141.019(1), 141.021)?
GIVEN `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income (on a joint return, the joint figure)
      `my interest from other states' bonds` IS A NUMBER @desc Interest on bonds of other states and their cities and counties
      `my taxable social security and railroad retirement` IS A NUMBER @desc Social security and railroad retirement benefits included in your federal AGI
      `my pension and retirement distributions` IS A NUMBER @desc Your own distributions from pensions, annuities, IRAs, 401(k) and other retirement plans included in federal AGI
      `my spouse's pension and retirement distributions` IS A NUMBER @desc On a joint return, your spouse's own such distributions; otherwise 0
      `my active duty military pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Military pay received while on active duty in the US Armed Forces
      `my pre-1998 government retirement annuities` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of federal or Kentucky local government retirement annuities that is excluded because it accrued before 1998
      `my other Kentucky inclusions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other amount KRS 141.019(1) adds (not worked out here); usually 0
      `my other Kentucky exclusions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other amount KRS 141.019(1) excludes (not worked out here); usually 0
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my Kentucky adjusted gross income` MEANS
    `Kentucky adjusted gross income` (`Adjusted gross income facts` WITH
        `federal adjusted gross income` IS `my federal adjusted gross income`
        `interest from sister states' obligations` IS `my interest from other states' bonds`
        `social security and railroad retirement benefits subject to federal tax` IS `my taxable social security and railroad retirement`
        `pension exclusion of the taxpayer` IS `the 141.019(1)(g) exclusion` `my pension and retirement distributions`
        `pension exclusion of the spouse on the return` IS `the 141.019(1)(g) exclusion` `my spouse's pension and retirement distributions`
        `active duty military pay` IS `my active duty military pay`
        `government retirement annuities excluded by 141.021` IS `my pre-1998 government retirement annuities`
        `other inclusions` IS `my other Kentucky inclusions`
        `other exclusions` IS `my other Kentucky exclusions`)

§§ `The family size threshold`

-- The threshold is the HHS poverty guideline for the family unit size of 141.066(1)(e). The guidelines are a base figure
-- for one person and an increment for each further person; the person states both.
@export Which family size does Kentucky use for my filing threshold and family size credit (KRS 141.066(1)(e))?
GIVEN `we are a married couple living together, filing jointly or on a combined return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a married couple living together who file a joint return, or separately on a combined return
      `my qualifying children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying children (IRC s152(c)) you have, including a child in the household you cannot claim because of the divorced-parent rules
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What family size is used for my threshold` MEANS
    `the family unit size for the threshold` `we are a married couple living together, filing jointly or on a combined return` `my qualifying children`

§§ `Must I file, and by when`

@export Must I file a Kentucky income tax return (KRS 141.180(2))?
GIVEN `I am a Kentucky resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a Kentucky resident
      `we are a married couple living together, filing jointly or on a combined return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a married couple living together (your income is combined for this test)
      `my qualifying children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying children (IRC s152(c)) you have
      `my modified gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your modified gross income: the greater of your federal AGI plus other states' bond interest, or your Kentucky AGI (combined, for a couple living together)
      `my self-employment gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross income from self-employment
      `I have Kentucky-source income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a nonresident: whether you have gross income from Kentucky sources
      `my total gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total gross income from all sources
      `the poverty guideline for one person` IS A NUMBER @desc The HHS poverty guideline for a household of one, as available on June 30 of the tax year
      `the guideline increment per extra person` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the HHS poverty guidelines add for each additional person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I file a Kentucky return` IF
    `shall file a return` `I am a Kentucky resident` `my modified gross income` `my self-employment gross income` `I have Kentucky-source income` `my total gross income` threshold
    WHERE
        size MEANS `the family unit size for the threshold` `we are a married couple living together, filing jointly or on a combined return` `my qualifying children`
        threshold MEANS `the poverty guideline for one person` PLUS (`the guideline increment per extra person` TIMES (size MINUS 1))

@export By what date must I file my Kentucky return and pay the tax (KRS 141.160(1), 141.220)? Payment is due on this date even if the time to file is extended.
GIVEN `the month my tax year ends` IS A NUMBER @desc The month your tax year ends, 1 to 12 (12 for a calendar year)
      `the year my tax year ends` IS A NUMBER @desc The year your tax year ends
GIVETH A DATE
`When are my Kentucky return and tax due` MEANS `the 141.160 due date` `the month my tax year ends` `the year my tax year ends`

§§ `How much do I owe, or get back`

@export How much Kentucky income tax do I owe for the year, or how much is refunded, after credits and the tax already withheld (KRS 141.019, 141.020, 141.066, 141.067, 141.069, 141.0205)?
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The tax year (2024 or later)
      `the General Assembly cut the rate for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For 2027 or later: whether the General Assembly has enacted a rate reduction under KRS 141.020(2)(g) for this tax year
      `I was a Kentucky resident all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a Kentucky resident for the whole year
      `I paid income tax to another state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid income tax to another state on income also taxed by Kentucky
      `my Kentucky adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Kentucky adjusted gross income (KRS 141.019(1))
      `I take the standard deduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you take the Kentucky standard deduction rather than itemizing (a married couple living together must both do the same)
      `the standard deduction for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The Kentucky standard deduction for the year, as published by the Department of Revenue
      `my Kentucky itemized deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Kentucky itemized deductions: federal itemized deductions without taxes, medical care, most losses, moving and miscellaneous deductions
      `people on the return aged 65 or older` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you and (on a joint return) your spouse were 65 or older before the end of the year
      `people on the return who are blind` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you and your spouse were blind at the end of the year
      `people on the return in the Kentucky National Guard` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you and your spouse were members of the Kentucky National Guard at the end of the year
      `we are a married couple living together, filing jointly or on a combined return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a married couple living together who file a joint return or separately on a combined return
      `I am single, or married filing separately with my spouse not in the household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you file single, or married filing separately while your spouse did not live in your household during the year
      `my qualifying children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying children (IRC s152(c)) you have
      `my modified gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your modified gross income (the greater of federal AGI plus other states' bond interest, or Kentucky AGI)
      `the poverty guideline for one person` IS A NUMBER @desc The HHS poverty guideline for a household of one, as available on June 30 of the tax year
      `the guideline increment per extra person` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the HHS poverty guidelines add for each additional person
      `my federal tuition credit for Kentucky undergraduate study` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal education credit (IRC s25A) for undergraduate tuition at a Kentucky institution
      `I file a separate return from my spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are married and file a separate return (not a joint or combined return)
      `my federal child and dependent care credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal child and dependent care credit allowed to you (IRC s21)
      `Kentucky tax withheld and estimated tax paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Kentucky income tax withheld from your pay and any Kentucky estimated tax you paid
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What do I owe or get back in Kentucky` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the 141.020(2) rate` `the tax year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered` `taxable years before 2024 are not encoded`
    WHEN JUST rate THEN
        IF `the tax year` AT LEAST 2027 AND `the General Assembly cut the rate for the year`
        THEN `not covered` `a rate reduction enacted by the General Assembly for taxable years from 2027 (141.020(2)(g)) is not encoded`
        ELSE IF (NOT `I was a Kentucky resident all year`)
             THEN `not covered` `the tax of a nonresident or part-year resident is not encoded: 141.020(4) and (6) tax only Kentucky-source income for the nonresident period, and the method of computing it is not stated in the deposited text`
             ELSE IF `I paid income tax to another state`
                  THEN `not covered` `the credit for income tax paid to another state (141.070) is not encoded`
                  ELSE `answered` ((`tax after the nonrefundable credits` (rate TIMES taxableNet) individual familyPct tuition care) MINUS `Kentucky tax withheld and estimated tax paid`)
    WHERE
        taxableNet MEANS `net income` `my Kentucky adjusted gross income` `I take the standard deduction` `the standard deduction for the year` `my Kentucky itemized deductions`
        individual MEANS `the 141.020(3) credits` `people on the return aged 65 or older` `people on the return who are blind` `people on the return in the Kentucky National Guard` FALSE FALSE
        qualifies MEANS `we are a married couple living together, filing jointly or on a combined return` OR `I am single, or married filing separately with my spouse not in the household`
        size MEANS `the family unit size for the threshold` `we are a married couple living together, filing jointly or on a combined return` `my qualifying children`
        threshold MEANS `the poverty guideline for one person` PLUS (`the guideline increment per extra person` TIMES (size MINUS 1))
        familyPct MEANS IF qualifies THEN `the family size credit percentage` `my modified gross income` threshold ELSE 0
        tuition MEANS `the 141.069 tuition credit` `my federal tuition credit for Kentucky undergraduate study` `I file a separate return from my spouse`
        care MEANS `the 141.067 care credit` `my federal child and dependent care credit`

@export What share of my Kentucky tax does the family size tax credit take away (KRS 141.066(3))? 1 means all of it.
GIVEN `my modified gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your modified gross income (the greater of federal AGI plus other states' bond interest, or Kentucky AGI)
      `we are a married couple living together, filing jointly or on a combined return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a married couple living together who file a joint or combined return
      `my qualifying children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying children (IRC s152(c)) you have
      `the poverty guideline for one person` IS A NUMBER @desc The HHS poverty guideline for a household of one, as available on June 30 of the tax year
      `the guideline increment per extra person` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the HHS poverty guidelines add for each additional person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What share does the family size credit take` MEANS
    `the family size credit percentage` `my modified gross income` threshold
    WHERE
        size MEANS `the family unit size for the threshold` `we are a married couple living together, filing jointly or on a combined return` `my qualifying children`
        threshold MEANS `the poverty guideline for one person` PLUS (`the guideline increment per extra person` TIMES (size MINUS 1))
